      \"id\": \"F8\",\n   138\t      \"what\": {\"population\": \"Meta Platforms\", \"measure\": \"AI capital expenditures\", \"scope\": \"company total\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"},\n   139\t      \"kind\": \"source\",\n   140\t      \"basis\": \"third_party\",\n   141\t      \"value\": 130,\n   142\t      \"low\": null,\n   143\t      \"high\": null,\n   144\t      \"unit\": \"USD bn\",\n   145\t      \"evidence_id\": \"e3686\",\n   146\t      \"quote_number\": \"$130 billion\",\n   147\t      \"qualifier\": \"none\",\n   148\t      \"inputs\": null,\n   149\t      \"operation\": null,\n   150\t      \"basis_text\": null,\n   151\t      \"rests_on\": null,\n   152\t      \"outcome_for\": [],\n   153\t      \"reference_for\": []\n   154\t    },\n   155\t    {\n   156\t      \"id\": \"F9\",\n   157\t      \"what\": {\"population\": \"Microsoft\", \"measure\": \"capital expenditures\", \"scope\": \"company total\", \"period\": \"FY2026 Q3\"},\n   158\t      \"kind\": \"source\",\n   159\t      \"basis\": \"reported\",\n   160\t      \"value\": 30.88,\n   161\t      \"low\": null,\n   162\t      \"high\": null,\n   163\t      \"unit\": \"USD bn\",\n   164\t      \"evidence_id\": \"e922\",\n   165\t      \"quote_number\": \"$30.88 billion\",\n   166\t      \"qualifier\": \"none\",\n   167\t      \"inputs\": null,\n   168\t      \"operation\": null,\n   169\t      \"basis_text\": null,\n   170\t      \"rests_on\": null,\n   171\t      \"outcome_for\": [],\n   172\t      \"reference_for\": []\n   173\t    },\n   174\t    {\n   175\t      \"id\": \"F10\",\n   176\t      \"what\": {\"population\": \"five largest AI hyperscalers\", \"measure\": \"data-center capex\", \"scope\": \"combined\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"},\n   177\t      \"kind\": \"source\",\n   178\t      \"basis\": \"third_party\",\n   179\t      \"value\": 800,\n   180\t      \"low\": null,\n   181\t      \"high\": null,\n   182\t      \"unit\": \"USD bn\",\n   183\t      \"evidence_id\": \"e5376\",\n   184\t      \"quote_number\": \"$800 billion\",\n   185\t      \"qualifier\": \"nearly\",\n   186\t      \"inputs\": null,\n   187\t      \"operation\": null,\n   188\t      \"basis_text\": null,\n   189\t      \"rests_on\": null,\n   190\t      \"outcome_for\": [],\n   191\t      \"reference_for\": []\n   192\t    },\n   193\t    {\n   194\t      \"id\": \"F11\",\n   195\t      \"what\": {\"population\": \"four largest AI hyperscalers\", \"measure\": \"capital expenditures\", \"scope\": \"combined total\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"},\n   196\t      \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n   197\t      \"basis\": \"forecast\",\n   198\t      \"value\": 745,\n   199\t      \"low\": null,\n   200\t      \"high\": null,\n   201\t      \"unit\": \"USD bn\",\n   202\t      \"evidence_id\": null,\n   203\t      \"quote_number\": null,\n   204\t      \"qualifier\": null,\n   205\t      \"inputs\": null,\n   206\t      \"operation\": null,\n   207\t      \"basis_text\": \"I forecast spending at the upper end of the Zacks range. Alphabet, Amazon and Meta lifted their full-year plans, and Microsoft's reported quarter and strong cloud demand support a rising spending pace. Amazon's higher memory costs lift dollar spending even if equipment volumes rise more slowly. Project delays and grid constraints make the higher plan tally less likely to be fully spent this year. The annual estimates already reflect the company plans, so I use those plans to choose where spending lands within the estimates.\",\n   208\t      \"rests_on\": [\"F2\", \"F3\", \"F4\", \"F5\", \"F6\", \"F7\", \"F9\", \"e4404\", \"e4406\", \"e122\", \"e5292\"],\n   209\t      \"outcome_for\": [],\n   210\t      \"reference_for\": []\n   211\t    },\n   212\t    {\n   213\t      \"id\": \"F12\",\n   214\t      \"what\": {\"population\": \"four largest AI hyperscalers\", \"measure\": \"capital expenditures\", \"scope\": \"combined outside data centers\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"},\n   215\t      \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n   216\t      \"basis\": \"forecast\",\n   217\t      \"value\": 25,\n   218\t      \"low\": null,\n   219\t      \"high\": null,\n   220\t      \"unit\": \"USD bn\",\n   221\t      \"evidence_id\": null,\n   222\t      \"quote_number\": null,\n   223\t      \"qualifier\": null,\n   224\t      \"inputs\": null,\n   225\t      \"operation\": null,\n   226\t      \"basis_text\": \"I estimate a $25 billion deduction for spending outside data centers. The four-company AI infrastructure tally is close to my total-capex forecast, and Meta's AI capex estimate is close to the midpoint of its companywide guidance. Those comparisons support a small deduction. I allow room for different spending mixes across the companies and for some AI infrastructure spending to fall outside data centers. The passages do not give a company-by-company split.\",\n   227\t      \"rests_on\": [\"F1\", \"F7\", \"F8\", \"F11\"],\n   228\t      \"outcome_for\": [],\n   229\t      \"reference_for\": []\n   230\t    },\n   231\t    {\n   232\t      \"id\": \"F13\",\n   233\t      \"what\": {\"population\": \"four largest AI hyperscalers\", \"measure\": \"data-center capex\", \"scope\": \"combined\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"},\n   234\t      \"kind\": \"computed\",\n   235\t      \"basis\": \"forecast\",\n   236\t      \"value\": 720,\n   237\t      \"low\": null,\n   238\t      \"high\": null,\n   239\t      \"unit\": \"USD bn\",\n   240\t      \"evidence_id\": null,\n   241\t      \"quote_number\": null,\n   242\t      \"qualifier\": null,\n   243\t      \"inputs\": [\"F11\", \"F12\"],\n   244\t      \"operation\": \"difference\",\n   245\t      \"basis_text\": null,\n   246\t      \"rests_on\": null,\n   247\t      \"outcome_for\": [\"v6\"],\n   248\t      \"reference_for\": []\n   249\t    }\n   250\t  ],\n   251\t  \"answers\": [\n   252\t    {\n   253\t      \"view_id\": \"v6\",\n   254\t      \"shape\": \"forecast\",\n   255\t      \"rung\": 4,\n   256\t      \"reference_unavailable\": null,\n   257\t      \"reasons\": \"I forecast $720 billion of calendar 2026 data-center capex, in rung 4. The closest market reference, more than $730 billion of AI infrastructure spending for the same four companies, points to rung 4 and uses a broader spending label. Raised company outlooks, Microsoft's reported spending and strong cloud demand support $745 billion of total capex. After my $25 billion deduction for spending outside data centers, the forecast stays above $700 billion. Grid constraints and delayed projects put the lower boundary at risk, but the delay tally covers U.S. projects across developers and gives no amount attributable to these four companies' 2026 capex. NVIDIA's nearly $800 billion estimate covers five companies and serves as a cross-check. The AWS GPU expansion is scheduled for 2027–2028 and gives no amount to add to 2026.\",\n   258\t      \"why\": null,\n   259\t      \"cites\": [\"e1947\", \"e5014\", \"e1856\", \"e2458\", \"e1254\", \"e1649\", \"e1549\", \"e3686\", \"e922\", \"e4404\", \"e4406\", \"e122\", \"e5292\", \"e5376\", \"e5150\"],\n   260\t      \"pushes\": [\n   261\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e1947\", \"push\": \"none\"},\n   262\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e5014\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"},\n   263\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e1856\", \"push\": \"none\"},\n   264\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e2458\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n   265\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e1254\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n   266\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e1649\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n   267\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e1549\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n   268\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e3686\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n   269\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e922\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n   270\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e4404\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n   271\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e4406\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n   272\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e122\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"},\n   273\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e5292\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"},\n   274\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e5376\", \"push\": \"none\"},\n   275\t        {\"evidence_id\": \"e5150\", \"push\": \"none\"}\n   276\t      ],\n   277\t      \"theme_pushes\": []\n   278\t    }\n   279\t  ]\n   280\t}controls/K-unresolved-justified.json\n     1\t{\"figures\": [{\"id\": \"F1\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"four largest AI hyperscalers\", \"measure\": \"total capital expenditure\", \"scope\": \"combined\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"}, \"kind\": \"source\", \"basis\": \"third_party\", \"value\": null, \"low\": 720, \"high\": 745, \"unit\": \"USD bn\", \"evidence_id\": \"e5014\", \"quote_number\": \"$720 billion to $745 billion\", \"qualifier\": \"roughly\", \"inputs\": null, \"operation\": null, \"basis_text\": null, \"rests_on\": null, \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}, {\"id\": \"F2\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"four largest AI hyperscalers\", \"measure\": \"total capital expenditure\", \"scope\": \"combined\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"}, \"kind\": \"source\", \"basis\": \"third_party\", \"value\": 760, \"low\": null, \"high\": null, \"unit\": \"USD bn\", \"evidence_id\": \"e2458\", \"quote_number\": \"$760 billion\", \"qualifier\": \"none\", \"inputs\": null, \"operation\": null, \"basis_text\": null, \"rests_on\": null, \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}, {\"id\": \"F3\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"Alphabet\", \"measure\": \"total capital expenditure\", \"scope\": \"company-wide\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"}, \"kind\": \"source\", \"basis\": \"guidance\", \"value\": null, \"low\": 195, \"high\": 205, \"unit\": \"USD bn\", \"evidence_id\": \"e1254\", \"quote_number\": \"$195 billion to $205 billion\", \"qualifier\": \"none\", \"inputs\": null, \"operation\": null, \"basis_text\": null, \"rests_on\": null, \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}, {\"id\": \"F4\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"Amazon\", \"measure\": \"total capital expenditure\", \"scope\": \"company-wide\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"}, \"kind\": \"source\", \"basis\": \"guidance\", \"value\": 220, \"low\": null, \"high\": null, \"unit\": \"USD bn\", \"evidence_id\": \"e1649\", \"quote_number\": \"$220 billion\", \"qualifier\": \"none\", \"inputs\": null, \"operation\": null, \"basis_text\": null, \"rests_on\": null, \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}, {\"id\": \"F5\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"Meta Platforms\", \"measure\": \"total capital expenditure\", \"scope\": \"company-wide\", \"period\": \"FY2026\"}, \"kind\": \"source\", \"basis\": \"guidance\", \"value\": null, \"low\": 125, \"high\": 145, \"unit\": \"USD bn\", \"evidence_id\": \"e1549\", \"quote_number\": \"$125 billion to $145 billion\", \"qualifier\": \"none\", \"inputs\": null, \"operation\": null, \"basis_text\": null, \"rests_on\": null, \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}, {\"id\": \"F6\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"Meta Platforms\", \"measure\": \"AI capital expenditure\", \"scope\": \"company-wide\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"}, \"kind\": \"source\", \"basis\": \"third_party\", \"value\": 130, \"low\": null, \"high\": null, \"unit\": \"USD bn\", \"evidence_id\": \"e3686\", \"quote_number\": \"$130 billion\", \"qualifier\": \"none\", \"inputs\": null, \"operation\": null, \"basis_text\": null, \"rests_on\": null, \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}, {\"id\": \"F7\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"Microsoft\", \"measure\": \"total capital expenditure\", \"scope\": \"company-wide\", \"period\": \"FY2026 Q3\"}, \"kind\": \"source\", \"basis\": \"reported\", \"value\": 30.88, \"low\": null, \"high\": null, \"unit\": \"USD bn\", \"evidence_id\": \"e922\", \"quote_number\": \"$30.88 billion\", \"qualifier\": \"none\", \"inputs\": null, \"operation\": null, \"basis_text\": null, \"rests_on\": null, \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}, {\"id\": \"F8\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"Microsoft\", \"measure\": \"year-over-year capital expenditure growth\", \"scope\": \"company-wide\", \"period\": \"FY2026 Q3\"}, \"kind\": \"source\", \"basis\": \"reported\", \"value\": 84, \"low\": null, \"high\": null, \"unit\": \"%\", \"evidence_id\": \"e922\", \"quote_number\": \"84%\", \"qualifier\": \"none\", \"inputs\": null, \"operation\": null, \"basis_text\": null, \"rests_on\": null, \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}, {\"id\": \"F9\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"four largest AI hyperscalers\", \"measure\": \"AI infrastructure spending\", \"scope\": \"combined\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"}, \"kind\": \"source\", \"basis\": \"guidance\", \"value\": 730, \"low\": null, \"high\": null, \"unit\": \"USD bn\", \"evidence_id\": \"e1947\", \"quote_number\": \"$730 billion\", \"qualifier\": \"more than\", \"inputs\": null, \"operation\": null, \"basis_text\": null, \"rests_on\": null, \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}, {\"id\": \"F10\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"five largest AI hyperscalers\", \"measure\": \"data-center capex\", \"scope\": \"combined\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"}, \"kind\": \"source\", \"basis\": \"third_party\", \"value\": 800, \"low\": null, \"high\": null, \"unit\": \"USD bn\", \"evidence_id\": \"e5376\", \"quote_number\": \"$800 billion\", \"qualifier\": \"nearly\", \"inputs\": null, \"operation\": null, \"basis_text\": null, \"rests_on\": null, \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}, {\"id\": \"F11\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"four largest AI hyperscalers\", \"measure\": \"total capital expenditure\", \"scope\": \"combined\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"}, \"kind\": \"estimate\", \"basis\": \"forecast\", \"value\": 745, \"low\": null, \"high\": null, \"unit\": \"USD bn\", \"evidence_id\": null, \"quote_number\": null, \"qualifier\": null, \"inputs\": null, \"operation\": null, \"basis_text\": \"I expect combined spending to land near the high end of the Zacks range. The Alphabet, Amazon and Meta revisions and Microsoft's reported spending growth support a strong pace. Amazon's higher memory costs also lift dollar spending. Project delays and grid connection constraints lead me to assume that some planned spending slips, keeping the forecast below the higher published plan.\", \"rests_on\": [\"F1\", \"F2\", \"F3\", \"F4\", \"F5\", \"F7\", \"F8\", \"e122\", \"e5292\"], \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}, {\"id\": \"F12\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"four largest AI hyperscalers\", \"measure\": \"data-center share of total capital expenditure\", \"scope\": \"combined\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"}, \"kind\": \"estimate\", \"basis\": \"forecast\", \"value\": 90, \"low\": null, \"high\": null, \"unit\": \"%\", \"evidence_id\": null, \"quote_number\": null, \"qualifier\": null, \"inputs\": null, \"operation\": null, \"basis_text\": \"I estimate that data centers account for 90% of combined capital expenditure. Zacks identifies AI infrastructure as a large use of the group's spending, and the Meta AI capex estimate is close to its total capex guidance. I use that comparison as evidence of a high share and allow for other capital spending across all four companies. The packet gives no group-wide data-center split.\", \"rests_on\": [\"F1\", \"F5\", \"F6\", \"e4404\"], \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}, {\"id\": \"F13\", \"what\": {\"population\": \"four largest AI hyperscalers\", \"measure\": \"data-center capex\", \"scope\": \"combined\", \"period\": \"CY2026\"}, \"kind\": \"computed\", \"basis\": \"forecast\", \"value\": 670.5, \"low\": null, \"high\": null, \"unit\": \"USD bn\", \"evidence_id\": null, \"quote_number\": null, \"qualifier\": null, \"inputs\": [\"F11\", \"F12\"], \"operation\": \"share\", \"basis_text\": null, \"rests_on\": null, \"outcome_for\": [], \"reference_for\": []}], \"answers\": [{\"view_id\": \"v6\", \"shape\": \"unresolved\", \"rung\": null, \"reference_unavailable\": null, \"reasons\": \"The question asks for the four companies' data-center capital expenditure, and the rung turns on whether it reaches $700 billion. The passages give the four companies' total capital expenditure (about $720-745 billion, e5014; tracked near $745 billion and $760 billion, e1856, e2458), AI-infrastructure spending of more than $730 billion (e1947), and data-center capex of nearly $800 billion for five companies (e5376). None of them gives the four companies' data-center share: a total, a broader AI category and a five-company figure do not settle whether the four-company data-center figure is above or below $700 billion, since a share of about 94% of the total is the dividing line. So the rung cannot be settled from these passages.\", \"why\": \"The question asks for the four companies' data-center capital expenditure, and the rung turns on whether it reaches $700 billion. The passages give the four companies' total capital expenditure (about $720-745 billion, e5014; tracked near $745 billion and $760 billion, e1856, e2458), AI-infrastructure spending of more than $730 billion (e1947), and data-center capex of nearly $800 billion for five companies (e5376). None of them gives the four companies' data-center share: a total, a broader AI category and a five-company figure do not settle whether the four-company data-center figure is above or below $700 billion, since a share of about 94% of the total is the dividing line. So the rung cannot be settled from these passages.\", \"cites\": [\"e5014\", \"e2458\", \"e1254\", \"e1649\", \"e1549\", \"e3686\", \"e922\", \"e4404\", \"e1947\", \"e5376\", \"e122\", \"e5292\", \"e5150\"], \"pushes\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"e5014\", \"push\": \"none\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e2458\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e1254\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e1649\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e1549\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e3686\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e922\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e4404\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e1947\", \"push\": \"none\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e5376\", \"push\": \"none\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e122\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e5292\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"e5150\", \"push\": \"none\"}], \"theme_pushes\": []}]}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
