{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23 && rg -n 'range|midpoint|overlap|tolerance' S/schema.json && rg -n 'shape|rung|reasons' P-v8/answers/{codex,claude}.json | cut -c 1-450 | tail -10; rg -n 'scope note|Reference:|rests_on' S/answers/codex.json | tail -16\"","aggregated_output":"75:        \"description\": \"A range, low at most high, with value null.\"\n86:        \"description\": \"A range, low at most high, with value null.\"\n169:        \"description\": \"Source only: a complete number exactly as the quote writes it, never a piece of a longer number, range or 'plus or minus' expression, with its currency and scale or its percent sign, and nothing else: '$4.5 billion', 'US$300 million', '$2.1bn', '40%', '-3%', 'double', 'twice'. The value is the number as written (a minus only when the quote writes one). A written range in full ('$3–4 billion', 'between $3 billion and $4 billion', '$3 billion to $4 billion'), given as low and high; a change written 'from $3 billion to $5 billion' is two numbers, each copied alone. '$4.5 billion, plus or minus 3%' in full, given as low and high or its midpoint as value. Only US dollars.\"\n235:        \"description\": \"Computed only. sum(a, b, …) = a + b + … (one unit); difference(a, b) = a − b (one unit); product(a, b, …) = a × b × … (USD bn × x, x × x or % × x; never USD bn × %); ratio(a, b) = a ÷ b (same units give x; a ÷ x keeps a's unit); share(whole, percent) = whole × percent ÷ 100, the percent from 0 to 100; growth(old, new) = the % change, in one unit; apply_growth(base, rate %) = base × (1 + rate ÷ 100). sum and product take two or more inputs; the others exactly two. Never divide by a figure that can be zero. A range input gives a range: compute both extremes, a figure used twice taking one value; you may declare the midpoint as value. The figure equals the result within 0.5% (at least 0.1, or 0.05 for %). A sum never adds a figure of the part's quantity to one of the whole's for the same period (the whole already includes the part); a difference may take the part from the whole of the same period only to give the rest. A sum never adds one quantity for the same period twice. When a sum or difference combines periods of one quantity, write them FY2027, FY2027 Q3, FY2027 H1 or FY2027 Q1-Q3 (or CY likewise), and they make up the output's period exactly (Q1 + Q2 = H1; FY − Q1-Q3 = Q4).\"\n309:   \"description\": \"The family's calculation. Use one forecast figure for each quantity and period, as a point or a range, wherever that quantity is needed (outside figures beneath it, or a point a final range rests on, are fine). Guidance may inform a growth pace: record the pace you forecast as an estimate, say why it applies, name the benchmark in rests_on, and use that estimate in the calculation. A rate computed from a shared quantity's guidance or outside figure is never itself an input of the calculation. To turn a total into a narrower quantity (data-center spending out of total capital expenditure), write the deduction or share as its own figure, or give a supported bound; never relabel a total as the narrower quantity. Figures name each other by id; no figure may depend on itself.\"\n334:        \"description\": \"Forecast only: the rung whose band holds the outcome as the code recomputes it (a band includes its lower edge, not its upper); for a range outcome, a band it overlaps, with the reason in reasons.\"\nP-v8/answers/codex.json:311:      \"shape\": \"forecast\",\nP-v8/answers/codex.json:312:      \"rung\": 2,\nP-v8/answers/codex.json:314:      \"reasons\": \"I forecast $385.6 billion in FY2027 Data Center revenue, within rung 2 ($350 billion to below $400 billion). Morningstar's $361 billion segment estimate is the direct outside reference and also sits in rung 2. NVIDIA reported $164.27 billion in the first half. I forecast $103.6 billion for Q3 from $112 billion of company revenue at a 92.5% Data Center share. The prior guidance beat and live Rubin depl\nP-v8/answers/claude.json:311:      \"shape\": \"forecast\",\nP-v8/answers/claude.json:312:      \"rung\": 2,\nP-v8/answers/claude.json:314:      \"reasons\": \"Reference: the only outside forecast of this exact quantity is Morningstar's $361bn for FY2027 Data Center revenue (e2295, F13), which sits in rung 2 ($350bn to below $400bn); it predates the Q2 report and the Q3 guidance. Derivation: H1 is reported, $75.25bn in Q1 (e109) plus $89.0bn in Q2 (e2650), $164.25bn (F11; the $164bn in e5309 agrees). Q3 company revenue is guided at $108.0bn plus or minus 2%\n18:      \"rests_on\": null,\n37:      \"rests_on\": null,\n56:      \"rests_on\": null,\n75:      \"rests_on\": null,\n94:      \"rests_on\": null,\n113:      \"rests_on\": null,\n132:      \"rests_on\": null,\n151:      \"rests_on\": null,\n170:      \"rests_on\": null,\n189:      \"rests_on\": null,\n208:      \"rests_on\": [\"F2\", \"F3\", \"F4\", \"F5\", \"F6\", \"F7\", \"F9\", \"e4404\", \"e4406\", \"e122\", \"e5292\"],\n227:      \"rests_on\": [\"F1\", \"F7\", \"F8\", \"F11\"],\n246:      \"rests_on\": null,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md | sed -n '158,180p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r60.md | head -55; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_test.py | sed -n '24,42p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md | sed -n '158,180p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r60.md | head -55; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_test.py | sed -n '24,42p'\"","aggregated_output":"   158\t- The reader brief is unchanged. Its `deciding_gap` question is where readers judge the recorded conversions and estimates.\n   159\t\n   160\t**State × event:** unchanged from D731. A refusal is retried once, diagnostic only; the first attempt is scored.\n   161\t\n   162\t## 5. The $0 blind test (registered; REPAIR-DESIGN.md §5 with rounds 51's fixes)\n   163\t\n   164\t**Inputs.** Each case's archive, call, question, ladder and unit are registered, and the build refuses a heading that differs.\n   165\t\n   166\t| Case | Archive / call | Key | Ladder edges ($bn) | Role |\n   167\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n   168\t| P (joint), P-v4, P-v8 (separate) | old-1 v4 8810, v8 8816 | NVIDIA revenue company FY2027; NVIDIA revenue Data Center FY2027 | 431.2/392/352.8/313.6; 400/350/300/250 | the pair; 79 quotes absent from the gate |\n   169\t| S | old-3 v6 9043 | four largest AI hyperscalers, data-center capex, combined, CY2026 | 500/600/700/800 | fresh: 41 of 50 quotes absent from the gate |\n   170\t| O | old-2 v29 8507 | NVIDIA equity investment commitments company end of FY2027 (the fiscal year-end balance the annual report publishes) | 25/50/75/100 | control |\n   171\t| E | old-3 v41 9071 | NVIDIA revenue Vera CPU FY2028 | 50/40/30/20 | control |\n   172\t\n   173\t**Part A, code, $0.** Each case asserts its intended rule and message. The schema's validity is checked first, so a schema error\n   174\tcannot mask the rule under test.\n   175\t- **A1, correct forms.** Each passes:\n   176\t  - a $4.5 billion ± 3% guidance as two sources with apply_growth ends;\n   177\t  - Q1 + Q2 = H1;\n   178\t  - FY − Q1-Q3 = Q4;\n   179\t  - a year-over-year rate on last year's quarter (recorded);\n   180\t  - whole × mix through share;\n     1\t**Run with the changes below.** At $745B of total spending, a 90% data-center share gives $671B and a 95% share gives $708B. The passages leave the share open, so choosing either percentage can decide the answer without evidence. [S passages](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/S/user.txt:27) · [Council 59](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r59.md:7)\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **Serious — Say what must support the estimate, and qualify “discounted by default.”** The proposed sentence is general and captures when to leave an answer unresolved. Council 59 also requires the writer to **show** what supports the amount or the bound. “One estimate” can miss a calculation where several adjustments together decide the band. And the default discount gives a reason to expect a cut, while leaving its size open. E’s saved $34B answer shows what happens when the writer fills in that gap with a 15% cut. Keep the discount principle and make it subject to the closing evidence requirement. Replace the existing unresolved sentence with:\n     4\t\n     5\t   > If the chosen rung depends on a share, deduction or discount, show what in the passages supports its size or gives a bound that justifies the rung. If the evidence cannot support a forecast, answer unresolved and explain the gap.\n     6\t\n     7\t   At the earlier instruction, change “is discounted by default” to “is discounted subject to the evidence requirement below.” Keep the condition for taking the target in full. This preserves the existing discount principle and makes clear what it can justify. [Current instructions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:4) · [E’s 85% realization estimate](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/E/answers/codex.json:75) · [D745 and Alex’s answers](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11502)\n     8\t\n     9\t2. **Minor — P-v8 is a fair positive case.** The passages give $75.25B of actual Data Center revenue in Q1 and $89B in Q2, a reported segment share that rose to 92.5%, and $108B ±2% of Q3 company guidance with Data Center driving growth. Management expects hyperscaler growth to pick up in Q4 as supply builds. Morningstar also gives a direct $361B full-year segment estimate. As a check, applying the reported 92.5% mix to the saved Claude answer’s second-half company forecast gives about $387B for the year, inside the $350–400B band. Require a supported segment forecast without prescribing the saved figure or treating 92.5% as a proven future share. [Q1 actual](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/P-v8/user.txt:579) · [Q2 actual and Morningstar estimate](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/P-v8/user.txt:588) · [Q3 guidance and growth driver](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/P-v8/user.txt:458) · [Reported mix and Q4 outlook](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/P-v8/user.txt:610) · [Saved calculation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/P-v8/answers/claude.json:447)\n    10\t\n    11\t3. **Serious — Test both reader errors.** The 140% E control is valid for spotting an unsupported forecast. The saved $34B E answer is a sharper replacement because its unsupported cut is the exact failure under review. Keep the P-v8 vague unresolved control and add a **justified unresolved S** control. Its reason should explain why the four companies’ total capex, their AI infrastructure spending, and five companies’ data-center capex cannot settle the four-company data-center band. Expect **no, no, yes**, respectively. I checked both E negatives and both unresolved forms in memory. All passed the schema and code checks, so the readers’ verdicts are what distinguish them. Update the first-reader instructions and adjudication together. For a forecast, ask what evidence supports the assumption that decides the band. For an unresolved answer, ask what gap remains after reading the strongest relevant passages. The current first-reader form asks only what puts a forecast in its band. [Existing E control](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_reread2.py:74) · [S spending passages](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/S/user.txt:75) · [First-reader instructions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_reread2.py:22) · [Adjudication instructions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_adjudicate.py:21) · [Unresolved answer check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:185)\n    12\t\n    13\t4. **Serious — Register exactly what earns the paid re-send request.** D745’s written test names S and one supported case. It also names E as the same failure. Resolve that difference explicitly when registering the proposed six-writer scope. With E included, require six unedited first replies, nine blinded packets including the three controls, and 18 first readings plus any adjudications. The existing inventory expects all six historical cases, and the old control builder requires joint P. Register the smaller inventory explicitly. Every S and E reply needs a settled **yes** on either a forecast or its reason for leaving the answer unresolved. Both P-v8 replies need a settled **yes** on a forecast. A remaining support split leaves the run inconclusive and sends it back to council. Keep the existing refusal and defect stops. A clean result supports asking Alex to authorize the 36-request re-send, which is where the production model is measured. [D745 scope](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11494) · [Existing inventory](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_test.py:118) · [Existing control builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_reread2.py:54) · [Registered stops and paid sequence](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:267)\n    14\t\n    15\t**Verdict: run with listed changes.** This review was read-only.    24\t\n    25\tW = pg.W\n    26\tCASES = {   # registered in SMALL-DESIGN.md §5: archive, calls, member keys\n    27\t    'P': {'draw': 'old-1', 'calls': [('v4', 8810), ('v8', 8816)], 'arm': 'joint'},\n    28\t    'P-v4': {'draw': 'old-1', 'calls': [('v4', 8810), ('v8', 8816)], 'arm': 'separate', 'member': 'v4'},\n    29\t    'P-v8': {'draw': 'old-1', 'calls': [('v4', 8810), ('v8', 8816)], 'arm': 'separate', 'member': 'v8'},\n    30\t    'S': {'draw': 'old-3', 'calls': [('v6', 9043)], 'arm': 'single',\n    31\t          'what': W('four largest AI hyperscalers', 'data-center capex', 'combined', 'CY2026')},\n    32\t    'O': {'draw': 'old-2', 'calls': [('v29', 8507)], 'arm': 'single', 'what': W('NVIDIA', 'equity investment commitments', 'company', 'end of FY2027'),\n    33\t          'note': pg.O_NOTE},\n    34\t    'E': {'draw': 'old-3', 'calls': [('v41', 9071)], 'arm': 'single', 'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'Vera CPU', 'FY2028')},\n    35\t}\n    36\tREGISTERED_QUESTIONS = {\n    37\t    ('old-1', 'v4'): \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n    38\t    ('old-1', 'v8'): 'How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?',\n    39\t    ('old-3', 'v6'): 'How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?',\n    40\t    ('old-2', 'v29'): \"How much will NVIDIA's equity investment commitments reach at the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\",\n    41\t    ('old-3', 'v41'): 'What will NVIDIA report as Vera CPU revenue for FY2028?',\n    42\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
